    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `ageBand` derivation for owners. When a `POST /api/owners` request includes `birthDate` (ISO date), the returned owner now carries an `ageBand` of `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+), computed against the owner's `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `birthDate` (`format: date`) input to the `OwnerFields` schema, and a read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` schema. These regenerate `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` (with a nested `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum`).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, column `birth_date`) field with getter/setter so the value is persisted and available for mapping.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `toAgeBand` mapping that computes the band via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` (`<18 \u2192 MINOR`, `<65 \u2192 ADULT`, else `SENIOR`), returning `null` when `birthDate` or `registrationDate` is absent. MapStruct auto-maps `birthDate` on both directions.\n\n4. **Schema/data SQL** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to all four `schema.sql` variants (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) and appended the matching `NULL` to the hsqldb `data.sql` positional owner seed inserts (the profile the tests run under).\n\nThe existing `coreDerivesAgeBand` acceptance test (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`) and the full suite pass: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nNote: the `birthDate` is echoed back on reads since it lives on the shared `OwnerFields` schema \u2014 harmless and consistent with how other input fields (e.g. `registrationDate`, `postcode`) are surfaced.",
